From: OCCTSwift ecosystem <noreply@secondmouse.au>
Subject: [PATCH] Modeling Data - BinTools sets read the name of a table into a buffer of that
 size and no further

BinTools_ShapeSet, LocationSet, Curve2dSet, CurveSet and SurfaceSet each begin their Read of a
table with char buffer[255]; IS >> buffer; and compare the token with the name of the table
("Locations", "Curve2ds", "Curves", "Surfaces", "TShapes"). An unbounded formatted read into a
char array writes the whole token: a 300 byte token overwrites the stack silently, a 4 KB token
terminated the process (SIGTRAP), and a 1 MiB token did not return in 60 s. Every reader that
hands a stream to BinTools_ShapeSet::Read reaches it, among them
BinLDrivers_DocumentRetrievalDriver for the SHAPE_SECTION_POS entry of a binary OCAF file, whose
table of contents names any offset in the file.

The read now carries the buffer's size (std::setw), so a longer token is cut. It is then not the
name of the table, and each Read already throws Standard_Failure for that.

Tracked as SecondMouseAU/OCCTSwift#3489, follow-up to #3486.

---
diff --git a/src/ModelingData/TKBRep/BinTools/BinTools_ShapeSet.cxx b/src/ModelingData/TKBRep/BinTools/BinTools_ShapeSet.cxx
--- a/src/ModelingData/TKBRep/BinTools/BinTools_ShapeSet.cxx
+++ b/src/ModelingData/TKBRep/BinTools/BinTools_ShapeSet.cxx
@@ -13,6 +13,7 @@
 // Alternatively, this file may be used under the terms of Open CASCADE
 // commercial license or contractual agreement.
 
+#include <iomanip>
 #include <BinTools.hxx>
 #include <BinTools_Curve2dSet.hxx>
 #include <BinTools_ShapeSet.hxx>
@@ -426,7 +427,8 @@
   //-----------------------------------------
 
   char buffer[255];
-  IS >> buffer;
+  // a token longer than the buffer is cut, and then is not the name of the table
+  IS >> std::setw(sizeof(buffer)) >> buffer;
   if (IS.fail() || strcmp(buffer, "TShapes"))
   {
     Standard_SStream aMsg;
